14. Key Takeaways
•	Asset = what you protect.
•	Threat = what can cause harm.
•	Vulnerability = weakness.
•	Risk = potential harm/loss associated with a threat exploiting a vulnerability.
•	Impact = how bad; Likelihood = how probable.
•	Risk ≈ Likelihood × Impact is a useful simplified interview model.
•	Risk treatment: Mitigate, Avoid, Transfer, Accept.
•	Vulnerability ≠ Risk — this is a key interview distinction.
